# Cloudflare reads this at deploy time. vinext generates a minimal version of
# this file only when one is not already here, so this replaces it — keep the
# /assets/* rule.

# Content-hashed by the bundler; the name changes when the bytes do.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# A symbol mask is immutable by construction: `name--weight.png` is one drawing
# from one macOS release, and a new release adds files rather than editing them.
# This is the whole traffic story — 7,988 files, and the visitor's second visit
# should fetch none of them.
/symbols/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# The three pictures that live at a fixed path. They were falling through to the
# default, which is `max-age=0, must-revalidate` — so og.png, half a megabyte of
# it, was fetched in full by every social scraper on every share, and the favicon
# was revalidated on every visit. Not `immutable`, because unlike /symbols/* the
# name does not change when the bytes do: these are redrawn by
# scripts/render_sfsymbols.swift and keep their filenames. An hour is long enough
# to carry a link doing the rounds, short enough that a redraw goes live the same
# afternoon.
/og.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600, stale-while-revalidate=86400
/favicon.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600, stale-while-revalidate=86400
/bettermapit.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600, stale-while-revalidate=86400

# The reader pastes AI conversations and internal specs into this page, so the
# promise that none of it leaves the browser is enforced here rather than just
# claimed. The directives that carry that promise are `connect-src 'self'` (no
# fetch, XHR, WebSocket or beacon to anywhere else) and `img-src 'self' data:`
# (an image URL is an exfiltration channel too). A browser enforces both; it
# does not have to take our word for anything.
#
# `script-src` and `style-src` allow inline out of necessity, not preference:
# the SSR output carries 8 inline <script> blocks holding the React payload, and
# the tile geometry is passed as inline style props. Without unsafe-inline the
# page never hydrates and the site is blank. Hashes are not an option — the
# payload changes every build — and vinext has no nonce support. The XSS risk
# that buys back is small here: no server, no accounts, and nothing a visitor
# types is ever shown to anyone else.
#
# These comments sit outside the rule block on purpose — an indented `#` is not
# reliably a comment to Cloudflare's parser, it can read as a broken header.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data:; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; connect-src 'self'; font-src 'self'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
